%
% Backward goal: list membership, negative case — the gmeow:listContains backing (#1009 §5).
% Reuses the listMember/2 rdf:first/rdf:rest walk from contains.logic. The ground goal
% asks whether ex:absent is a member of the list (x y z); it is not, so the goal
% fails and returns empty bindings, status ok.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions/').
:- prefix(rdf, 'http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#').
ex:listMember(L, X) :- rdf:first(L, X).
ex:listMember(L, X) :- rdf:rest(L, R), ex:listMember(R, X).
?- ex:listMember(ex:l0, ex:absent).
